./docs/deployment-modes.md:26:Each request gets a fresh MCP server instance, Streamable HTTP transport, Hevy client, and exercise-template cache [[4]](https://github.com/chrisdoc/hevy-mcp/blob/47eac6bd864bbfc1d66bbd48881df895e1a4214e/README.md#L348-L349) [[5]](https://github.com/chrisdoc/hevy-mcp/blob/47eac6bd864bbfc1d66bbd48881df895e1a4214e/CONTRIBUTING.md#L282-L293). The Worker validates the supplied Hevy API key with Hevy on each request, does not store it, and forwards it to Hevy only as the required `api-key` header [[6]](https://github.com/chrisdoc/hevy-mcp/blob/47eac6bd864bbfc1d66bbd48881df895e1a4214e/README.md#L446-L448). There is no shared user session or persisted key [[7]](https://github.com/chrisdoc/hevy-mcp/blob/47eac6bd864bbfc1d66bbd48881df895e1a4214e/README.md#L349-L350).
